<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna `condfold noreturn`: a chain of tests that all branch to one call that
    does not return, `if ((r = f()) != 0 || (r = g()) != 0) fatal(r, ..);`,
    prints as one `if` over the `||` chain with the call as its body and the
    rest of the function after it.  The function is structured inside the main
    loop while each call block still holds its stack bookkeeping, so upstream's
    BlockBasic::isComplex declines every later test and the chain prints as a
    ladder of nested `if`s with the call after all of them.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality", option condfold (default noreturn).

    The images are decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/
    fatalchain_gcc_O2_x86_64 and fatalchain_gcc_O0_x86_64 (fatalchain.c,
    gcc 11.4 -O2 -fno-reorder-blocks-and-partition and -O0), loaded whole;
    `option noreturn fatal` states what the whole-binary run infers.  reply
    is only the chain, twice has two chains after a single test, wide's second
    test makes four calls, more than the condstmts cap of three statements in
    front of a folded test, and compose (-O0) has the rest of the function
    after the chain.

    Pass 1 runs with `option condfold off` and prints the ladders.  Pass 2
    (`option condfold noreturn`, the default) prints each chain as one `if`
    with the call as its body; wide keeps its ladder.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/fatalchain_gcc_O2_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>option noreturn fatal</com>
  <com>option condfold off</com>
  <com>load function reply</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function twice</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option condfold noreturn</com>
  <com>load function reply</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function twice</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function wide</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/fatalchain_gcc_O0_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>option noreturn fatal</com>
  <com>option condfold off</com>
  <com>load function compose</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option condfold noreturn</com>
  <com>load function compose</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #1: off prints reply as a ladder that returns innermost" min="1" max="1">^        return;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #2: the default prints reply's chain as one condition" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(\(v1\) \|\| \(v1 = put\(a0,v[0-9] &amp; 0xffffffff\), v1\)\) \|\| \(v1 = put\(a0,v[0-9] &amp; 0xffffffff\), v1\)\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #3: the default makes the no-return call the body" min="1" max="1">^    fatal\(v1,"reply"\); // no-return$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #4: off nests twice's second chain inside the first" min="1" max="1">^      fatal\(v1,"second"\); // no-return$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #5: the default prints twice's first chain as one if" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(v1\) \|\| \(v1 = put\(a0,v3 &amp; 0xffffffff\), v1\)\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #6: the default prints twice's second chain as one if" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(v1\) \|\| \(v1 = put\(a0,\*a0\), v1\)\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #7: the default prints the rest of twice after the chains" min="1" max="1">^  return \*a0;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #8: wide's test with four calls in front keeps its ladder" min="1" max="1">^  fatal\(v1,"wide"\); // no-return$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #9: off nests compose's rest inside the -O0 ladder" min="1" max="1">^        sink = \*a0;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #10: the default prints compose's -O0 chain as one condition" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(\(v1\) \|\| \(v1 = put\(a0,a1\), v1\)\) \|\| \(v1 = put\(a0,a2\), v1\)\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FATALCHAIN #11: the default prints compose's rest after the chain" min="1" max="1">^  sink = \*a0;$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
